  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd the exact 2D nesting kernel to `camcraft_geometry::nesting`.\nPreserve the existing raster API.\nCompute NFPs and IFPs on the `geo2d::SCALE` grid.\nPlace parts deterministically with bottom-left-fill.\nSupport cut-side clearances, open chains, rotations, mirrors, nested holes, and multiple sheets.\nReport quantities, net-area utilization, used bounds, waste regions, and named refusals.\nRefuse overflowing quantities and requests above 10,000 instances.\nAdd no dependencies or ECS access.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe geometry crate exposed a raster filter but lacked an exact NFP/IFP placer.\nThe earlier clean-room kernel remained on a held branch after an upstream build failure.\nThis change integrates that CamCraft work and tightens exact clearance and quantity checks.\nThe algorithm sources are Bennell and Oliveira (EJOR 2008), Burke et al. (OR 2006), and Burke et al. (EJOR 2007).\nThe decision record explains the choices and alternatives.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe pinning build failed on unchanged upstream base `f3b0e195503466db86b0ff0b15dbf614153e1bb4` because the nesting API was absent.\nThe final focused run passed 66 tests: 51 library tests and 15 nesting integration tests.\n\nPins:\n\n- `deterministic_irregular_l_shapes_nest_without_overlap`\n- `places_small_part_inside_large_part_hole_with_full_clearance`\n- `swept_open_chains_and_cut_sides_nest_cleanly`\n- `multi_sheet_overflow_and_exact_per_sheet_counts`\n- `refuses_non_finite_negative_and_oversized_inputs_by_name`\n- `router_single_slot_mode_fits_shared_channel_and_refuses_under_sized_gap`\n- `fixed_step_rotation_and_mirror_unlock_tight_placements`\n- `allow_mirror_places_chiral_part_in_cavity_and_circular_hole_accepts_inner_part`\n- `batch_30_irregular_parts_is_deterministic_and_zero_overlap`\n- `cut_side_inflations_leave_exact_uncut_gap`\n- `chiral_cavity_on_larger_sheet_finds_zero_slack_seam`\n- `multi_level_parts_in_holes_and_open_slit_clearance`\n- `refuses_malformed_parts_and_edge_cases_by_name`\n- `refuses_unbounded_and_overflowing_requested_quantities`\n- `refuses_requested_quantity_sum_overflow`\n- `nesting::candidates::tests::exact_check_refuses_micron_escape_from_hole`\n- `nesting::candidates::tests::exact_check_refuses_sub_epsilon_overlap`\n\nNine independent runtime mutations failed their pins and passed after restoration.\nThey disabled hole containment, tiny-overlap rejection, the router gap guard, negative-input rejection, quantity overflow handling, the quantity cap, outer kerf inflation, internal NFP seams, and filled-hole obstacles.\nCopying upstream `nesting.rs` back also failed the API pins.\nRestoring the implementation passed all 66 focused tests again.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed.\nGeometry selected the batch fallback: 936 steps, zero failures.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nWorkspace all-targets clippy also passed within the gate.\nThe branch tree stayed unchanged during validation.\nThe shared upstream reference advanced during the long gate; the tested branch uses base `f3b0e1955`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe branch changes no `.nc` or `.cl` files.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nApp and motion heavy lanes were planned but not run.\nThey must run before the PR becomes ready.\nThe PR remains a draft.\nThe kernel has no UI, posting, or machine execution integration in this issue.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found in the open-PR file checks.\n\nChangelog: Add deterministic true-shape nesting with cut clearance, nested holes, multi-sheet accounting, and named input refusals.\n\nEffort: max; no escalation.\n\nFixes #2158\n",
